Buck was preparing for his assault on the castle. No
problem, with -36 AC, reflection and two sources of MR! But,
no BoH. In his trek down from his main stash on DL 13 (the
only altar in the main dungeon) he became stressed just as
he got to the castle level. While making a new stash in an
extra sack, a master lich popped in.

Well, here's the plan, drop the bag, stand on the upstairs
so the lich can't escape and two weapon Magicbane (to avoid
curses) with the +6 long sword. The damn lich was just a
knight's move away but he wouldn't come fight. Three times
he summoned nasties.

Buck wasn't worried, at first. Twice assorted minotaurs,
jabberwocks and dragons teamed up to get Buck down to about
110/159 HP. He finally whipped out the +7 Mojo and fired off
a couple of sleep spells before things could really get out
of hand.

Boy, those minotaurs and jabberwocks hit hard! The dragons,
trolls and giants in the throne room on the level above
couldn't get him below 140.
